    "humanReview": "User qualitative approval recorded; numeric ratings remain unmeasured.",
    "solution": "Place the echo on the upper isolated perch. Catch the lower ring, pay out for the low tally, then reel in through the leftward return. Pump right. During the next rising rightward arc, press Echo while continuing to hold Grab: the swap now releases the old tether automatically and preserves the swing velocity. Jump + Echo remains an optional higher departure. The receiving shelf is three tiles wider and one tile lower than the previous revision.",
    "nearestExisting": "p131 The Citadel and F19 The Weight Must Stay relocate a prepared machinery launch. Here the launch is made by changing a rope length and steering a pendulum after a low objective; the direction and vertical component at release determine whether the relocated arc clears the gulf.",
    "novelty": "There is no dash fallback. The low tally asks for an extended outward arc; the exit asks for a shortened rising return. The same controllable pendulum must supply both trajectories, and the echo transports its velocity across an otherwise lethal beam partition. The upper route is deliberately beyond an ordinary jump from the echo perch.",
    "designNotes": "Fixed a real engine bug: echo-swapping while still hooked previously retained the old spatial tether, causing a huge pull toward the old ring. Successful swaps now call normal hook release before teleportation; blocked swaps leave the tether intact. The canonical route deliberately keeps Grab held through the swap. Human-keyboard coverage verifies the same path.",
